{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id486915120"}, "name":{"label":"SpringBaby413"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-08T18:13:56-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"484.0.0"}, "id":{"label":"14644051034"}, "title":{"label":"Doesn’t Track Accurately"}, "content":{"label":"I have logged over 1,500 miles in runs on this app. I have over 400 activites (runs) on this app. Needless to say, I was loyal for a long time. Maybe I didn’t care about my stats before, but now that i’m training for a race, I’ve become frustrated with the app for not accurately keeping track of my PR’s. And the support email is NO help. I have an activity on the app that states it’s my 5k PR at 17 minutes 41 seconds. On my Best Efforts page? The paced run I ran TODAY at 26 minutes. My best efforts puts my most recent run as my “best”, but it won’t acknowledge that I ran my actual best at 17:41. I’m trying to keep track of my splits for my race. If it just tosses any old run into my Best Efforts but wants to throw “your best 5k time yet!” in my face but not update the app correctly, I need to move onto a different platform. I’m proud to have ran a 5k under 18 minutes and the app can’t even properly track that. I’ve taken this issue to support countless times and the have an automated response that doesn’t help every single time. All that said, if you want accurate running results look for an app elsewhere.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=426826309&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
